# A Windows CI run only means something if it sees the same bytes as everybody
# else. Git for Windows installs with core.autocrlf=true by default and the
# GitHub windows-latest image does not override it, so without this line a
# checkout there rewrites every LF to CRLF on the way to disk.
#
# That is not cosmetic in this repository. The importers build their fixtures
# out of multi-line raw string literals — `crates/remoter-import/src/**/tests.rs`
# — so the line endings are part of the data under test, and three protocol
# crates scan their own source with `include_str!` to prove no diagnostic in the
# file names a keystroke. Both read differently out of a CRLF checkout.
#
# No tracked file contains a carriage return today. This normalises nothing; it
# keeps it that way.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Told explicitly rather than left to content detection, because these are read
# byte-for-byte by the bundler and a heuristic that guessed wrong once would be
# a corrupt installer icon nobody could explain.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
